1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:18,707
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June fifth, which is Environment Day in Japan. It's a day to stop and think about the planet and how we treat it. In fact, all of June is treated as a month for the environment here. Let's listen.

2
00:00:19,307 --> 00:00:22,068
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:22,768 --> 00:00:27,568
[News] 6月5日は、「環境の日」です。

4
00:00:28,268 --> 00:00:34,268
[News] 環境の日は、地球の自然について考える日です。

5
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:41,256
[News] 日本では、6月を「環境月間」と呼んでいます。

6
00:00:41,956 --> 00:00:48,652
[News] この1か月、日本のいろいろな所で、イベントがあります。

7
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:54,512
[News] たとえば、町のごみを拾う活動があります。

8
00:00:55,212 --> 00:00:58,643
[News] 木を植えるイベントもあります。

9
00:00:59,344 --> 00:01:05,055
[News] 川や海をきれいにする活動も、人気があります。

10
00:01:05,756 --> 00:01:11,900
[News] 学校でも、子どもたちが環境について勉強します。

11
00:01:12,599 --> 00:01:17,808
[News] 今、世界では、暑い日が増えています。

12
00:01:18,507 --> 00:01:23,188
[News] プラスチックのごみも、大きな問題です。

13
00:01:23,888 --> 00:01:28,975
[News] レジ袋を使わない人も、増えてきました。

14
00:01:29,676 --> 00:01:35,147
[News] 一人一人ができることは、小さいかもしれません。

15
00:01:35,847 --> 00:01:42,640
[News] でも、ごみを減らしたり、電気を大切に使ったりできます。

16
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:48,500
[News] 買い物には、自分のかばんを持っていきましょう。

17
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:56,135
[News] 政府は、「みんなで環境のことを考えましょう」と話しています。

18
00:01:56,835 --> 00:01:58,468
[Host] Let's break it down.

19
00:01:59,067 --> 00:02:04,540
[Slow] 6月5日は、「環境の日」です。

20
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:07,691
[Host] June fifth is Environment Day.

21
00:02:08,292 --> 00:02:10,668
[Vocab] 環境

22
00:02:11,068 --> 00:02:17,139
[Host] It means environment — the natural world around us, the air, water, and land.

23
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:24,604
[Slow] 環境の日は、地球の自然について考える日です。

24
00:02:25,403 --> 00:02:29,123
[Host] Environment Day is a day to think about the Earth's nature.

25
00:02:29,723 --> 00:02:31,860
[Vocab] 自然

26
00:02:32,259 --> 00:02:38,475
[Host] It means nature. Think mountains, rivers, forests — the world not made by people.

27
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:44,979
[Slow] たとえば、町のごみを拾う活動があります。

28
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:50,075
[Host] For example, there are activities to pick up trash around town.

29
00:02:50,675 --> 00:02:52,620
[Vocab] ごみ

30
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:59,379
[Host] It means trash or garbage. A very everyday word you'll see on bins all over Japan.

31
00:02:59,979 --> 00:03:03,891
[Slow] 木を植えるイベントもあります。

32
00:03:04,692 --> 00:03:07,379
[Host] There are also events for planting trees.

33
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:10,139
[Vocab] 植える

34
00:03:10,539 --> 00:03:15,243
[Host] It means to plant — putting a tree or seed into the ground so it can grow.

35
00:03:15,843 --> 00:03:21,795
[Slow] 今、世界では、暑い日が増えています。

36
00:03:22,596 --> 00:03:26,243
[Host] Right now, hot days are increasing around the world.

37
00:03:26,843 --> 00:03:29,075
[Vocab] 世界

38
00:03:29,475 --> 00:03:34,852
[Host] It means world. Add it to a topic and you've zoomed out to the whole planet.

39
00:03:35,451 --> 00:03:40,780
[Slow] プラスチックのごみも、大きな問題です。

40
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,747
[Host] Plastic trash is also a big problem.

41
00:03:45,348 --> 00:03:47,604
[Vocab] 問題

42
00:03:48,003 --> 00:03:52,756
[Host] It means problem or issue. It's also the word for a question on a test.

43
00:03:53,355 --> 00:04:01,108
[Slow] でも、ごみを減らしたり、電気を大切に使ったりできます。

44
00:04:01,907 --> 00:04:06,252
[Host] But we can do things like reduce trash and use electricity carefully.

45
00:04:06,852 --> 00:04:09,156
[Vocab] 減らす

46
00:04:09,556 --> 00:04:14,355
[Host] It means to reduce or cut down. The opposite is to increase.

47
00:04:14,955 --> 00:04:22,875
[Slow] 政府は、「みんなで環境のことを考えましょう」と話しています。

48
00:04:23,675 --> 00:04:27,851
[Host] The government is saying, let's all think about the environment together.

49
00:04:28,451 --> 00:04:30,875
[Vocab] 考える

50
00:04:31,276 --> 00:04:36,795
[Host] It means to think or to consider. Here, to think things over carefully as a group.

51
00:04:37,396 --> 00:04:40,396
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

